    {
      "id": 12978,
      "hub_id": null,
      "version": "2.0.0",
      "description": "<h3>Overview</h3>\n<p>KeyHunter has been completely reworked in this release to provide a smarter, more natural way of finding keys without relying on hardcoded ID lists or breaking the overall loot flow.</p>\n<p>Instead of static configuration, keys and keycards are discovered dynamically from the game database. Their availability scales with player progression, meaning players at lower levels mostly encounter common keys, while higher-level players gradually gain access to rarer and more valuable ones. This creates a smoother sense of progression without sudden loot spikes.</p>\n<h3>Loot Behavior</h3>\n<p>Key spawns can optionally be influenced by map routing, allowing keys to appear more frequently on their associated locations.</p>\n<p>To prevent key flooding from destabilizing the economy, the mod also includes an automatic price adjustment system for traders and the flea market.</p>\n<p>Internally, keys are categorized by rarity tiers (Common, Rare, Super Rare, and Keycards), allowing the system to make more informed decisions about when and where keys should appear.</p>\n<h3>Important Notice</h3>\n<p>This version is a major rewrite compared to v1.x and is not compatible with previous configurations.\nPlease remove the old KeyHunter mod folder completely and extract the new version.</p>\n",
